      "title": "EU charges TikTok with failing to protect users’ mental health",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/06/eu-charges-tiktok-failure-to-protect-users-mental-health",
      "description": "<p>Regulator’s initial ruling says algorithm ‘can be harmful’ and led young and vulnerable viewers ‘down rabbit holes they can’t easily escape’</p><p></p><p>TikTok has been charged by the European Commission with failing to protect users’ mental health by exposing them to a relentless stream of content that risks worsening eating disorders and anxiety in a case that strikes at its business model.</p><p>Issuing a preliminary ruling on Friday, the EU regulator said TikTok’s algorithm “can be harmful” and was leading young and vulnerable users “down rabbit holes they cannot easily escape from”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/06/eu-charges-tiktok-failure-to-protect-users-mental-health\">Continue reading...</a>",
